{"seq":34,"at":"2026-10-23","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1580"},"reason":"A paragraph on Odin's wolves Geri and Freki (Grímnismál, Prose Edda, the heroic lays) joins his household before the ravens, with their row in the table; the introduction now counts six beings.","by":"fact-count-rework","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",94],["-","Five"],["+","Six"],["=",3],["-","these"],["+","them"],["=",1],["-","beings"],["+","recur"],["=",1],["+","through the poems, and most "],["=",784],["+","At his feet lie two wolves, Geri and Freki, whose names both mean something like \"the greedy one\". In the \"Grímnismál\" Odin feeds them all the meat from his table, for the god himself lives on wine alone; Snorri repeats the verse in the Prose Edda, and in the heroic lays the wolves roam the battlefield, greedy for the corpses of the fallen.\n\n"],["=",372],["+","Geri and Freki | the greedy ones | Odin's wolves |\n| "],["=",21]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",102],["-","Fünf"],["+","Sechs"],["=",1],["-","dieser"],["+","von"],["=",1],["-","Wesen"],["+","ihnen"],["=",1],["+","kehren in den Gedichten immer wieder, und die meisten "],["=",736],["+","Zu seinen Füßen liegen zwei Wölfe, Geri und Freki, deren Namen beide etwa „der Gierige“ bedeuten. In den „Grímnismál“ füttert Odin sie mit allem Fleisch von seinem Tisch, denn der Gott selbst lebt allein vom Wein; Snorri wiederholt die Strophe in der Prosa-Edda, und in den Heldenliedern streifen die Wölfe gierig nach den Leichen der Gefallenen über das Schlachtfeld.\n\n"],["=",354],["+","Geri und Freki | die Gierigen | Odins Wölfe |\n| "],["=",21]]},{"field":"bodyRu","diff":[["=",76],["-","Пять"],["+","Шесть"],["=",1],["-","таких"],["+","из"],["=",1],["-","существ"],["+","них"],["=",1],["-","перешли"],["+","снова"],["=",1],["+","и снова встречаются в песнях, и большинство перешло "],["=",708],["+","У его ног лежат два волка — Гери и Фреки, чьи имена означают примерно «жадный». В «Речах Гримнира» Один отдаёт им всё мясо со своего стола, ведь сам бог живёт одним вином; Снорри повторяет эту строфу в «Младшей Эдде», а в героических песнях волки рыщут по полю битвы, жадные до тел павших.\n\n"],["=",318],["+","Гери и Фреки | жадные | волки Одина |\n| "],["=",21]]}],"hash":"33207aa157e7"},
